{:adr-id "2608250000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-0892 — Peat Extraction Operations Coordination"
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :author "Cloud Itonami Contributors"
 :status :accepted
 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 0892 (Extraction of peat) had no prior actor implementation
  -- the registry entry pointed at a placeholder repo
  (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-B0892) that was never created. A prior sibling
  agent originally assigned this class under the mistaken assumption it
  was salt extraction verified the live registry first, found {:id
  \"0892\" :name \"Extraction of peat\"}, and correctly identified 0893
  (subsequently implemented via ADR-2607152700) as the true salt slot
  without touching 0892. This ADR's author independently re-verified
  {:id \"0892\" :name \"Extraction of peat\" :maturity :spec ...}
  against a fresh clone before proceeding. Fresh, from-scratch scaffold,
  built as part of a smaller, carefully verified batch after an earlier
  18-agent haiku batch's 61% defect rate. Module shape mirrors sibling
  cloud-itonami-isic-0893 (Extraction of salt)'s verified module shape,
  domain-adapted for peat extraction: ISIC 0892 covers both milled peat
  (mechanical harrowing/ridging/vacuum-harvesting) and sod/block-cut
  peat (cutting and lifting solid blocks from the bog face), so the
  demo site directory seeds one site of each kind deliberately."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Coordination-only actor. Closed four-op allowlist, all :effect
   :propose: log-extraction-record, schedule-extraction-operation,
   flag-environmental-concern (always escalates), coordinate-shipment.
   An op outside this set is the same failure mode as forbidden-scope
   content, not a separate carve-out."
  :governor-rules
  "Three HARD, permanent, un-overridable checks: (1) site-unverified --
   target site (site + environmental permit) must be independently
   :registered?/:verified? in the store, never trusted from the
   proposal's own claim; (2) effect-not-propose -- any :effect other
   than :propose is a claim to directly actuate outside governance; (3)
   scope-exclusion -- any proposal (any op) touching extraction-
   equipment-control (milled peat: milling-machine/harrowing-machine/
   ridging-machine/vacuum-harvester control; sod/block-cut peat: sod-
   cutting/block-cutting/baling-machine control) or bog-drainage/
   environmental-permit-issuing-authority territory (drainage-ditch
   control, sluice-gate control, water-table control, drainage-canal
   control, weir control, fire-suppression control, permit issuance,
   license suspension, compliance enforcement), evaluated
   unconditionally via a lower-cased EN+JA substring scan of the
   proposal's own content. Excluded terms are control-verb-qualified so
   legitimate flag-environmental-concern observations are never
   self-blocked -- exercised directly by
   legitimate-environmental-flag-is-not-scope-excluded. Escalation
   (soft): flag-environmental-concern always, low confidence (<0.6).
   peatops.phase independently agrees -- flag-environmental-concern
   never auto-commits at any phase."
  :module-shape
  "peatops.store (MemStore, string-keyed site directory seeded with a
   milled-peat site, a sod-peat site, and an unverified sod-peat site),
   advisor (PeatOpsAdvisor, mock + real-LLM seam via langchain.model,
   plus an :out-of-scope? test hook), governor (PeatExtractionGovernor),
   phase (0->3 rollout), operation (langgraph-clj StateGraph), sim (demo
   driver)."}
 :consequences
 ["Registry entry corrected in place (exact-text edit of the existing"
  " {:id \"0892\" ...} block): :repo/:business-id updated from the"
  " stale gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-B0892 placeholder to"
  " cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0892, :maturity :implemented,"
  " :required-technologies narrowed to [:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn"
  " :audit-ledger] (dropping :robotics/:telemetry -- coordination-only)"
  "Actor repo cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0892 scaffolded and"
  " pushed to main (d978ec6bb9a5eb265ecabd87c1186d362486dbd5)"
  "Test suite run directly by this session: Ran 45 tests containing 136"
  " assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors (both at push time and again from a"
  " fresh post-push clone). clj-kondo: 0 errors, 0 warnings."]
